# Windows null device file (created by some build tools)
nul
tmp

# Supabase CLI's local dev stack scratch dir (`supabase start`) -- secrets and
# bundled edge function output, regenerated every run, never meant to be
# committed or linted.
supabase/.temp
# Database dumps. `supabase db dump` writes these into the repo root by
# default, and a data dump carries auth.users password hashes, app_credentials
# bcrypt hashes and live app_sessions tokens -- the most sensitive rows on the
# platform. Ignored by pattern rather than by name so the next backup, whatever
# it is called, cannot be swept into a commit by `git add -A`. Keep them
# outside the repo if you can.
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash on purpose: an unanchored
# `*-data-*.sql` would also match anything under supabase/migrations/, so a
# future migration called something like `add-data-column.sql` would be
# silently untracked -- a far worse failure than the one being prevented.
/prod-*.sql
/*-schema-*.sql
/*-data-*.sql
/*.dump
